			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3140137">
									

<p>I enjoyed this quite a bit; the writing is clean, the concept intriguing, and the dialogue <em>extremely</em> well-polished. However (you could tell that was coming, probably &gt;_&gt;):</p>
<p>I feel like Dr. Cadence's insistence that SCP-3357-1 is responsible for the containment breach (and therefore the deaths) is both deeply unfair and highly manipulative. If you stick somebody in a cage and drop that cage in a mine-field, you can't really yell at them when they sneak free and something blows up. Especially if you never even told them about the mines!</p>
<p>That being said, one way to take it (and the way I took it) is that Dr. Cadence was just using SCP-3357-1's guilt against them to get more info. Even if this wasn't intended to be the case, the article's good enough otherwise to merit an upvote.</p>

							</div>

								
					
