<p>It makes me happy to know that you enjoyed the article.</p>
<p>The way I intended Dr. Cadence's blame of SCP-3357-1 to be taken was both as unfairly manipulative and as information-gathering. In my mind, she genuinely holds SCP-3357 partially at fault for the incident (she blames herself just as much, and she really is meant to be on psychiatric leave after what happened), but when Cadence realizes that the anomaly feels guilty, she takes advantage of that to squeeze something useful out of the interaction.</p>

