			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3149968">
									

<p>&#8212;fair enough, yeah, and in rereading it, I think it gets that across quite well &#8212; I originally took the psychiatric leave thing the wrong way; that it was meant to paint Dr. Cadence as a victim who was coming to push the blame (unrightfully) on SCP-3357-1's shoulders.</p>
<p>It makes much more sense to interpret it the way you're describing: Dr. Cadence was on psychiatric leave because of guilt and trauma, and &#8212; in struggling with that &#8212; she confronted the anomaly, projected some of her guilt onto them, and then discovered the anomaly was vulnerable to that angle&#8230; so she used it against them to get more information out of them.</p>
<p>tl;dr &#8212; the way you write it works splendidly, I was just over-reading.</p>

